{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc | sed -n '340,1185p'\"","aggregated_output":"   340\t\n   341\t(defn- issue\n   342\t  \"Send one query for owner to peer pkey. Returns [state' outcome]: with\n   343\t   no cookie held the query is a padded :ping whatever the purpose; a\n   344\t   :store additionally needs a fresh peer. A query the socket refused is\n   345\t   not recorded.\"\n   346\t  [state owner [host port :as pkey] purpose]\n   347\t  (let [cookie (get-in state [:cookies pkey])\n   348\t        op (case purpose\n   349\t             :lookup (if cookie :find :ping)\n   350\t             :fetch (if cookie :fetch :ping)\n   351\t             :store (if (and cookie (fresh? state pkey)) :store :ping))\n   352\t        q (mint-q state host port)\n   353\t        query {:op op, :q q, :owner owner, :pkey pkey, :purpose purpose,\n   354\t               :sent (:now state), :resent? false}\n   355\t        outcome (send-datagram! state host port\n   356\t                                (query-message state query cookie))]\n   357\t    (if (= :dao.stream/ok outcome)\n   358\t      [(assoc-in state [:queries [host port q]] query) outcome]\n   359\t      [state outcome])))\n   360\t\n   361\t\n   362\t(defn- owner-queries\n   363\t  [state owner]\n   364\t  (filter #(= owner (:owner %)) (vals (:queries state))))\n   365\t\n   366\t\n   367\t(defn- drop-owner\n   368\t  \"Forget an operation and every query it owns.\"\n   369\t  [state owner]\n   370\t  (-> state\n   371\t      (update (first owner) dissoc (second owner))\n   372\t      (update :queries\n   373\t              (fn [qs] (into {} (remove #(= owner (:owner (val %)))) qs)))))\n   374\t\n   375\t\n   376\t;; =============================================================================\n   377\t;; Lookup as state (section 6)\n   378\t;; =============================================================================\n   379\t\n   380\t(defn- new-op\n   381\t  \"A pending operation's lookup state: target, candidates (the table's\n   382\t   nearest entries and the bootstrap contacts), answered and dead sets,\n   383\t   and per-peer failed tries.\"\n   384\t  [state kind address]\n   385\t  (let [target (jing/segment-hash address)\n   386\t        known (into {}\n   387\t                    (map (fn [e] [[(:host e) (:port e)] e]))\n   388\t                    (kad/nearest (:table state) target kad/k))\n   389\t        boot (into {}\n   390\t                   (map-indexed (fn [i {:keys [host port]}]\n   391\t                                  [[host port]\n   392\t                                   {:host host, :port port, :rank i}]))\n   393\t                   (::bootstrap state))]\n   394\t    {:kind kind\n   395\t     :address address\n   396\t     :target target\n   397\t     :started (:now state)\n   398\t     :cands (merge boot known)\n   399\t     :answered #{}\n   400\t     :dead #{}\n   401\t     :failures {}}))\n   402\t\n   403\t\n   404\t(defn- add-cands\n   405\t  \"Merge the table's nearest entries into an op's candidates.\"\n   406\t  [state owner]\n   407\t  (let [record (op-record state owner)]\n   408\t    (update-in state\n   409\t               (conj owner :cands)\n   410\t               (fn [cands]\n   411\t                 (reduce (fn [cands e]\n   412\t                           (let [pkey [(:host e) (:port e)]]\n   413\t                             (if (:id (get cands pkey))\n   414\t                               cands\n   415\t                               (assoc cands pkey e))))\n   416\t                         cands\n   417\t                         (kad/nearest (:table state) (:target record) kad/k))))))\n   418\t\n   419\t\n   420\t(defn- window\n   421\t  \"The k nearest live candidates of an op, nearest first: id-bearing\n   422\t   candidates by XOR distance, then unproven contacts in their order.\"\n   423\t  [record]\n   424\t  (->> (:cands record)\n   425\t       (remove (fn [[pkey _]] (contains? (:dead record) pkey)))\n   426\t       (sort-by (fn [[_ c]]\n   427\t                  (if (:id c)\n   428\t                    [0 (kad/distance (:id c) (:target record))]\n   429\t                    [1 (or (:rank c) 0)])))\n   430\t       (take kad/k)\n   431\t       (map first)))\n   432\t\n   433\t\n   434\t(defn- lookup-done?\n   435\t  \"A lookup ends when k peers have answered or its candidates are\n   436\t   exhausted, with nothing of it outstanding.\"\n   437\t  [state owner]\n   438\t  (let [record (op-record state owner)]\n   439\t    (and (not-any? #(= :lookup (:purpose %)) (owner-queries state owner))\n   440\t         (or (>= (count (:answered record)) kad/k)\n   441\t             (every? #(contains? (:answered record) %) (window record))))))\n   442\t\n   443\t\n   444\t(defn- issue-lookup\n   445\t  \"Ask the nearest unasked candidates, at most alpha outstanding.\"\n   446\t  [state owner]\n   447\t  (let [record (op-record state owner)\n   448\t        mine (owner-queries state owner)\n   449\t        busy (set (map :pkey mine))\n   450\t        outstanding (count (filter #(= :lookup (:purpose %)) mine))\n   451\t        todo (->> (window record)\n   452\t                  (remove #(contains? (:answered record) %))\n   453\t                  (remove busy)\n   454\t                  (take (max 0 (- alpha outstanding))))]\n   455\t    (if (>= (count (:answered record)) kad/k)\n   456\t      state\n   457\t      (reduce (fn [state pkey]\n   458\t                (let [[state outcome] (issue state owner pkey :lookup)]\n   459\t                  (if (= :dao.stream/ok outcome)\n   460\t                    state\n   461\t                    (update-in state (conj owner :dead) conj pkey))))\n   462\t              state\n   463\t              todo))))\n   464\t\n   465\t\n   466\t(defn- targets\n   467\t  \"The proven entries nearest an op's target that it has not acted on,\n   468\t   are live for it, and have no query of it outstanding.\"\n   469\t  [state owner acted]\n   470\t  (let [record (op-record state owner)\n   471\t        busy (set (map :pkey (owner-queries state owner)))]\n   472\t    (->> (kad/nearest (:table state) (:target record) kad/k)\n   473\t         (map (fn [e] [(:host e) (:port e)]))\n   474\t         (remove #(contains? acted %))\n   475\t         (remove #(contains? (:dead record) %))\n   476\t         (remove busy))))\n   477\t\n   478\t\n   479\t;; =============================================================================\n   480\t;; Section 4: pending writes\n   481\t;; =============================================================================\n   482\t\n   483\t(defn- acknowledge\n   484\t  [state owner]\n   485\t  (let [{:keys [address ids sent]} (op-record state owner)]\n   486\t    (-> (reduce (fn [state [r verdict]]\n   487\t                  (answer state {:jing/request r, :jing/result verdict}))\n   488\t                state\n   489\t                ids)\n   490\t        (fact {::fact ::sent, ::address address, ::peers (count sent)})\n   491\t        (assoc-in (conj owner :acked?) true)\n   492\t        (assoc-in (conj owner :ids) []))))\n   493\t\n   494\t\n   495\t(defn- give-up-write\n   496\t  [state owner]\n   497\t  (let [{:keys [address ids sent local]} (op-record state owner)]\n   498\t    (-> (reduce (fn [state [r _]]\n   499\t                  (answer state\n   500\t                          {:jing/request r,\n   501\t                           :jing/unacknowledged ::too-few-peers}))\n   502\t                state\n   503\t                ids)\n   504\t        (unacknowledged address ::too-few-peers (count sent) local)\n   505\t        (drop-owner owner))))\n   506\t\n   507\t\n   508\t(defn- replicated\n   509\t  [state owner]\n   510\t  (let [{:keys [address sent confirmed]} (op-record state owner)]\n   511\t    (-> state\n   512\t        (fact {::fact ::replicated, ::address address,\n   513\t               ::peers (count sent), ::confirmed confirmed})\n   514\t        (drop-owner owner))))\n   515\t\n   516\t\n   517\t(defn- send-stores\n   518\t  \"Send the store toward fresh targets until `limit` peers are counted,\n   519\t   and ping stale ones, at most alpha pings outstanding. A peer counts\n   520\t   only when the socket answered :dao.stream/ok.\"\n   521\t  [state owner limit]\n   522\t  (loop [state state\n   523\t         todo (targets state owner (:sent (op-record state owner)))]\n   524\t    (let [record (op-record state owner)\n   525\t          pings (count (filter #(and (= :store (:purpose %))\n   526\t                                     (= :ping (:op %)))\n   527\t                               (owner-queries state owner)))]\n   528\t      (if (or (empty? todo) (>= (count (:sent record)) limit))\n   529\t        state\n   530\t        (let [pkey (first todo)]\n   531\t          (if (fresh? state pkey)\n   532\t            (let [[state outcome] (issue state owner pkey :store)]\n   533\t              (recur (if (= :dao.stream/ok outcome)\n   534\t                       (update-in state (conj owner :sent) conj pkey)\n   535\t                       (update-in state (conj owner :dead) conj pkey))\n   536\t                     (rest todo)))\n   537\t            (recur (if (< pings alpha)\n   538\t                     (first (issue state owner pkey :store))\n   539\t                     state)\n   540\t                   (rest todo))))))))\n   541\t\n   542\t\n   543\t(defn- replication-done?\n   544\t  [state owner]\n   545\t  (let [sent (:sent (op-record state owner))]\n   546\t    (and (lookup-done? state owner)\n   547\t         (empty? (owner-queries state owner))\n   548\t         (or (>= (count sent) kad/k)\n   549\t             (empty? (targets state owner sent))))))\n   550\t\n   551\t\n   552\t(defn- advance-write\n   553\t  \"Section 4.3: send toward known fresh peers until ack-peers are counted,\n   554\t   look up when too few are known, acknowledge the moment the count is\n   555\t   reached, then replicate best effort; not acknowledged at ack-ticks.\"\n   556\t  [state address]\n   557\t  (let [owner [:writes address]\n   558\t        state (update-in state (conj owner :started) #(or % (:now state)))\n   559\t        {:keys [started acked?]} (op-record state owner)\n   560\t        now (:now state)\n   561\t        late? (and now started (>= (- now started) (::ack-ticks state)))]\n   562\t    (cond\n   563\t      (and late? (not acked?)) (give-up-write state owner)\n   564\t      late? (replicated state owner)\n   565\t\n   566\t      (not acked?)\n   567\t      (let [state (-> (add-cands state owner)\n   568\t                      (send-stores owner (::ack-peers state)))]\n   569\t        (if (>= (count (:sent (op-record state owner))) (::ack-peers state))\n   570\t          (acknowledge state owner)\n   571\t          (issue-lookup state owner)))\n   572\t\n   573\t      :else\n   574\t      (let [state (-> (add-cands state owner)\n   575\t                      (send-stores owner kad/k)\n   576\t                      (issue-lookup owner))]\n   577\t        (if (replication-done? state owner)\n   578\t          (replicated state owner)\n   579\t          state)))))\n   580\t\n   581\t\n   582\t;; =============================================================================\n   583\t;; Section 4.5: pending gets\n   584\t;; =============================================================================\n   585\t\n   586\t(defn- finish-get\n   587\t  [state owner found-bytes reason]\n   588\t  (let [{:keys [address ids]} (op-record state owner)\n   589\t        state (reduce (fn [state r]\n   590\t                        (answer state\n   591\t                                (if found-bytes\n   592\t                                  {:jing/request r, :jing/found? true,\n   593\t                                   :jing/bytes (jing/bytes->base64\n   594\t                                                 found-bytes)}\n   595\t                                  (not-found-answer r))))\n   596\t                      state\n   597\t                      ids)]\n   598\t    (cond-> (drop-owner state owner)\n   599\t      reason (miss address reason))))\n   600\t\n   601\t\n   602\t(defn- advance-get\n   603\t  \"Section 4.5: look the digest up, fetch from proven candidates, at most\n   604\t   alpha outstanding; not found when exhausted or at get-ticks.\"\n   605\t  [state address]\n   606\t  (let [owner [:gets address]\n   607\t        state (update-in state (conj owner :started) #(or % (:now state)))\n   608\t        {:keys [started]} (op-record state owner)\n   609\t        now (:now state)]\n   610\t    (if (and now started (>= (- now started) (::get-ticks state)))\n   611\t      (finish-get state owner nil ::deadline)\n   612\t      (let [state (add-cands state owner)\n   613\t            fetching (count (filter #(= :fetch (:purpose %))\n   614\t                                    (owner-queries state owner)))\n   615\t            todo (take (max 0 (- alpha fetching))\n   616\t                       (targets state owner (:fetched (op-record state owner))))\n   617\t            state (reduce (fn [state pkey]\n   618\t                            (let [[state outcome]\n   619\t                                  (issue state owner pkey :fetch)]\n   620\t                              (if (= :dao.stream/ok outcome)\n   621\t                                state\n   622\t                                (update-in state (conj owner :dead)\n   623\t                                           conj pkey))))\n   624\t                          state\n   625\t                          todo)\n   626\t            state (issue-lookup state owner)]\n   627\t        (if (and (lookup-done? state owner)\n   628\t                 (empty? (owner-queries state owner))\n   629\t                 (empty? (targets state owner\n   630\t                                  (:fetched (op-record state owner)))))\n   631\t          (finish-get state owner nil ::exhausted)\n   632\t          state)))))\n   633\t\n   634\t\n   635\t;; =============================================================================\n   636\t;; Stage 2: traffic\n   637\t;; =============================================================================\n   638\t\n   639\t(defn- safe-q?\n   640\t  [q]\n   641\t  (and (integer? q) (<= 0 q max-safe-integer)))\n   642\t\n   643\t\n   644\t(defn- reply!\n   645\t  \"Send a reply to the observed source, carrying a cookie for it.\"\n   646\t  [state host port q body]\n   647\t  (send-datagram! state host port\n   648\t                  (merge {::v 1, :op :reply, :q q,\n   649\t                          :id (hex->bytes (::id state)),\n   650\t                          :cookie (cookie-for (epoch state) host port)}\n   651\t                         body))\n   652\t  state)\n   653\t\n   654\t\n   655\t(defn- verified-bytes\n   656\t  \"The canonical bytes a peer handed over for address, or nil: strict\n   657\t   decode, digest against the address, canonical decode -- the one ingress\n   658\t   check, dao.jing/accept-bytes!.\"\n   659\t  [address bs]\n   660\t  (try (jing/accept-bytes! address (jing/bytes->base64 bs))\n   661\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil)))\n   662\t\n   663\t\n   664\t(defn- serve-body\n   665\t  \"The reply body for a request that passed the gate, or nil to drop it.\n   666\t   With publish? false a :store is refused and a :fetch is not found.\"\n   667\t  [state host port m]\n   668\t  (let [address (:address m)\n   669\t        local (:local state)]\n   670\t    (case (:op m)\n   671\t      :ping {:ok true}\n   672\t\n   673\t      :find\n   674\t      (when (bytes-of? (:target m) id-length)\n   675\t        {:peers (->> (kad/nearest (:table state)\n   676\t                                  (bytes->hex (:target m))\n   677\t                                  (inc max-find-peers))\n   678\t                     (remove #(and (= host (:host %)) (= port (:port %))))\n   679\t                     (take max-find-peers)\n   680\t                     (mapv (fn [e]\n   681\t                             [(hex->bytes (:id e)) (:host e) (:port e)])))})\n   682\t\n   683\t      :store\n   684\t      (when (and (jing/segment-address? address)\n   685\t                 (wire/byte-payload? (:bytes m)))\n   686\t        {:ok (boolean\n   687\t               (when (::publish? state)\n   688\t                 (when-let [bs (verified-bytes address (:bytes m))]\n   689\t                   (contains? #{:inserted :present}\n   690\t                              ((:put-bytes-fn local) address bs)))))})\n   691\t\n   692\t      :fetch\n   693\t      (when (jing/segment-address? address)\n   694\t        (let [bs (when (::publish? state)\n   695\t                   ((:get-bytes-fn local) address nil))]\n   696\t          (if bs {:found true, :bytes bs} {:found false})))\n   697\t\n   698\t      nil)))\n   699\t\n   700\t\n   701\t(defn- on-request\n   702\t  \"The gate: a request without a valid cookie causes no work, and its only\n   703\t   possible response is the need-cookie reply, sent only when it encodes\n   704\t   no longer than the datagram that caused it.\"\n   705\t  [state host port m size]\n   706\t  (let [q (:q m)]\n   707\t    (cond\n   708\t      (not (and (safe-q? q) (bytes-of? (:id m) id-length))) state\n   709\t\n   710\t      (not (valid-cookie? state host port (:cookie m)))\n   711\t      (let [need {::v 1, :op :reply, :q q, :id (hex->bytes (::id state)),\n   712\t                  :cookie (cookie-for (epoch state) host port),\n   713\t                  :need-cookie true}]\n   714\t        (when (<= (byte-count (wire/encode need)) size)\n   715\t          (send-datagram! state host port need))\n   716\t        state)\n   717\t\n   718\t      :else\n   719\t      (let [state (prove state (bytes->hex (:id m)) host port)\n   720\t            body (serve-body state host port m)]\n   721\t        (if body (reply! state host port q body) state)))))\n   722\t\n   723\t\n   724\t(defn- hint\n   725\t  \"Record :find reply peers as candidates, never entries.\"\n   726\t  [state owner peers]\n   727\t  (reduce (fn [state p]\n   728\t            (let [[id h pt] (when (vector? p) p)]\n   729\t              (if (and (bytes-of? id id-length)\n   730\t                       (string? h)\n   731\t                       (integer? pt)\n   732\t                       (not= (bytes->hex id) (::id state))\n   733\t                       (not (get-in state (conj owner :cands [h pt]))))\n   734\t                (assoc-in state\n   735\t                          (conj owner :cands [h pt])\n   736\t                          {:id (bytes->hex id), :host h, :port pt})\n   737\t                state)))\n   738\t          state\n   739\t          (take max-find-peers (when (sequential? peers) peers))))\n   740\t\n   741\t\n   742\t(defn- route-reply\n   743\t  \"Route a matched, full reply to the operation that owns its query.\"\n   744\t  [state query m]\n   745\t  (let [owner (:owner query)\n   746\t        pkey (:pkey query)]\n   747\t    (if-not (op-record state owner)\n   748\t      state\n   749\t      (case (:op query)\n   750\t        :find (-> state\n   751\t                  (update-in (conj owner :answered) conj pkey)\n   752\t                  (hint owner (:peers m)))\n   753\t        :store (if (true? (:ok m))\n   754\t                 (update-in state (conj owner :confirmed) inc)\n   755\t                 state)\n   756\t        :fetch (let [address (:address (op-record state owner))\n   757\t                     bs (when (and (true? (:found m))\n   758\t                                   (wire/byte-payload? (:bytes m)))\n   759\t                          (verified-bytes address (:bytes m)))]\n   760\t                 (if bs\n   761\t                   (let [verdict ((:put-bytes-fn (:local state)) address bs)]\n   762\t                     (when-not (#{:inserted :present} verdict)\n   763\t                       (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing.dht: invalid local put result\"\n   764\t                                       {:address address, :result verdict})))\n   765\t                     (finish-get state owner bs nil))\n   766\t                   (update-in state (conj owner :fetched) conj pkey)))\n   767\t        state))))\n   768\t\n   769\t\n   770\t(defn- on-reply\n   771\t  \"A reply is matched by [observed source, :q] against a pending query sent\n   772\t   to that address; anything else is dropped. A need-cookie reply stores\n   773\t   the cookie and re-sends the query once, without consuming a try; a full\n   774\t   reply proves and freshens the peer.\"\n   775\t  [state host port m]\n   776\t  (let [qkey [host port (:q m)]\n   777\t        query (get-in state [:queries qkey])\n   778\t        pkey [host port]]\n   779\t    (cond\n   780\t      (not (and query\n   781\t                (bytes-of? (:id m) id-length)\n   782\t                (bytes-of? (:cookie m) cookie-length)))\n   783\t      state\n   784\t\n   785\t      (true? (:need-cookie m))\n   786\t      (let [state (assoc-in state [:cookies pkey] (:cookie m))]\n   787\t        (if (:resent? query)\n   788\t          state\n   789\t          (let [query (assoc query :resent? true :sent (:now state))]\n   790\t            (send-datagram! state host port\n   791\t                            (query-message state query (:cookie m)))\n   792\t            (assoc-in state [:queries qkey] query))))\n   793\t\n   794\t      :else\n   795\t      (-> state\n   796\t          (update :queries dissoc qkey)\n   797\t          (prove (bytes->hex (:id m)) host port)\n   798\t          (assoc-in [:cookies pkey] (:cookie m))\n   799\t          (assoc-in [:seen pkey] (:now state))\n   800\t          (route-reply query m)))))\n   801\t\n   802\t\n   803\t(defn- on-traffic\n   804\t  [state v]\n   805\t  (let [source (:dao.stream.datagram/source v)\n   806\t        host (:dao.stream.datagram/host source)\n   807\t        port (:dao.stream.datagram/port source)\n   808\t        b64 (:dao.stream.datagram/bytes v)\n   809\t        bs (when (and (string? host) (integer? port) (string? b64))\n   810\t             (try (jing/base64->bytes b64)\n   811\t                  (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n   812\t                    nil)))\n   813\t        m (when bs (decode-message bs))]\n   814\t    (if (and m (= 1 (get m ::v)))\n   815\t      (case (:op m)\n   816\t        :reply (on-reply state host port m)\n   817\t        (:ping :find :store :fetch)\n   818\t        (on-request state host port m (byte-count bs))\n   819\t        ;; :chunk and anything else: chunks are S3\n   820\t        state)\n   821\t      state)))\n   822\t\n   823\t\n   824\t;; =============================================================================\n   825\t;; Stage 3: requests\n   826\t;; =============================================================================\n   827\t\n   828\t(defn- get-request?\n   829\t  [v]\n   830\t  (and (map? v)\n   831\t       (= #{:jing/request :jing/get} (set (keys v)))\n   832\t       (jing/segment-address? (get v :jing/get))))\n   833\t\n   834\t\n   835\t(defn- put-request?\n   836\t  [v]\n   837\t  (and (map? v)\n   838\t       (= #{:jing/request :jing/put :jing/bytes} (set (keys v)))\n   839\t       (jing/segment-address? (get v :jing/put))))\n   840\t\n   841\t\n   842\t(defn- replicate-request?\n   843\t  [v]\n   844\t  (and (map? v)\n   845\t       (= #{::replicate} (set (keys v)))\n   846\t       (jing/segment-address? (get v ::replicate))))\n   847\t\n   848\t\n   849\t(def ^:private absent\n   850\t  \"The local-read sentinel: one opaque host object, never a keyword.\"\n   851\t  #?(:cljd (Object.)\n   852\t     :clj (Object.)\n   853\t     :cljs (js-obj)))\n   854\t\n   855\t\n   856\t(defn- solo?\n   857\t  [state]\n   858\t  (nil? (:datagrams state)))\n   859\t\n   860\t\n   861\t(defn- write-refusal\n   862\t  \"The at-once reason a write cannot become pending, or nil.\"\n   863\t  [state address]\n   864\t  (cond\n   865\t    (solo? state) ::solo\n   866\t    (not (::publish? state)) ::unpublished\n   867\t    (and (not (contains? (:writes state) address))\n   868\t         (>= (count (:writes state)) (::max-pending-writes state)))\n   869\t    ::busy))\n   870\t\n   871\t\n   872\t(defn- join-write\n   873\t  \"Create or join the one pending write for address; r (optional) waits on\n   874\t   it with its local verdict. A write already acknowledged answers r at\n   875\t   once.\"\n   876\t  [state address r verdict]\n   877\t  (let [record (or (get-in state [:writes address])\n   878\t                   (assoc (new-op state :write address)\n   879\t                          :ids [] :sent #{} :confirmed 0 :acked? false\n   880\t                          :local verdict))]\n   881\t    (cond\n   882\t      (nil? r) (assoc-in state [:writes address] record)\n   883\t      (:acked? record) (-> (assoc-in state [:writes address] record)\n   884\t                           (answer {:jing/request r, :jing/result verdict}))\n   885\t      :else (assoc-in state [:writes address]\n   886\t                      (update record :ids conj [r verdict])))))\n   887\t\n   888\t\n   889\t(defn- on-put\n   890\t  [state v]\n   891\t  (let [r (get v :jing/request)\n   892\t        address (get v :jing/put)\n   893\t        bs (try (jing/accept-bytes! address (get v :jing/bytes))\n   894\t                (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))]\n   895\t    (cond\n   896\t      ;; the one ingress check refused it: dropped, as serve-step does\n   897\t      (nil? bs) state\n   898\t\n   899\t      (oversize? (::max-message-bytes state) address bs)\n   900\t      (-> (answer state {:jing/request r, :jing/unacknowledged ::oversize})\n   901\t          (unacknowledged address ::oversize 0 nil))\n   902\t\n   903\t      :else\n   904\t      (let [verdict ((:put-bytes-fn (:local state)) address bs)]\n   905\t        (when-not (#{:inserted :present} verdict)\n   906\t          (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing.dht: invalid local put result\"\n   907\t                          {:address address, :result verdict})))\n   908\t        (if-let [reason (write-refusal state address)]\n   909\t          (-> (answer state {:jing/request r, :jing/unacknowledged reason})\n   910\t              (unacknowledged address reason 0 verdict))\n   911\t          (join-write state address r verdict))))))\n   912\t\n   913\t\n   914\t(defn- on-replicate\n   915\t  [state address]\n   916\t  (let [bs ((:get-bytes-fn (:local state)) address absent)\n   917\t        reason (cond\n   918\t                 (solo? state) ::solo\n   919\t                 (not (::publish? state)) ::unpublished\n   920\t                 (identical? absent bs) ::absent\n   921\t                 (oversize? (::max-message-bytes state) address bs) ::oversize\n   922\t                 :else (write-refusal state address))]\n   923\t    (if reason\n   924\t      (unacknowledged state address reason 0 nil)\n   925\t      (join-write state address nil nil))))\n   926\t\n   927\t\n   928\t(defn- on-get\n   929\t  [state v]\n   930\t  (let [r (get v :jing/request)\n   931\t        address (get v :jing/get)\n   932\t        bs ((:get-bytes-fn (:local state)) address absent)]\n   933\t    (cond\n   934\t      (not (identical? absent bs))\n   935\t      (answer state {:jing/request r, :jing/found? true,\n   936\t                     :jing/bytes (jing/bytes->base64 bs)})\n   937\t\n   938\t      (solo? state)\n   939\t      (-> (answer state (not-found-answer r)) (miss address ::solo))\n   940\t\n   941\t      (contains? (:gets state) address)\n   942\t      (update-in state [:gets address :ids] conj r)\n   943\t\n   944\t      (>= (count (:gets state)) (::max-pending-gets state))\n   945\t      (-> (answer state (not-found-answer r)) (miss address ::busy))\n   946\t\n   947\t      :else\n   948\t      (assoc-in state [:gets address]\n   949\t                (assoc (new-op state :get address) :ids [r] :fetched #{})))))\n   950\t\n   951\t\n   952\t(defn- on-request-value\n   953\t  [state v]\n   954\t  (cond\n   955\t    (get-request? v) (on-get state v)\n   956\t    (put-request? v) (on-put state v)\n   957\t    (replicate-request? v) (on-replicate state (get v ::replicate))\n   958\t    ;; a malformed request is dropped without answer\n   959\t    :else state))\n   960\t\n   961\t\n   962\t;; =============================================================================\n   963\t;; Stage 1 and the stream reads\n   964\t;; =============================================================================\n   965\t\n   966\t(defn- on-tick\n   967\t  \"Time as data: the newest dao.lease tick reading is now.\"\n   968\t  [state v]\n   969\t  (let [n (when (and (map? v) (= :dao.lease/tick (:dao.lease/event v)))\n   970\t            (:dao.lease/reading v))]\n   971\t    (if (number? n)\n   972\t      (update state :now #(if (and % (> % n)) % n))\n   973\t      state)))\n   974\t\n   975\t\n   976\t(defn- drain\n   977\t  \"Read `reader-key` from its cursor to blocked, at most budget values,\n   978\t   folding each through f. A gap adopts the recovery cursor and says so.\"\n   979\t  [state reader-key cursor-key stream-name budget f]\n   980\t  (loop [state state\n   981\t         left budget]\n   982\t    (let [reader (get state reader-key)\n   983\t          cursor (get state cursor-key)]\n   984\t      (cond\n   985\t        (contains? stream/standard-anchors cursor)\n   986\t        (let [r (stream/cursor reader cursor)]\n   987\t          (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   988\t            (recur (assoc state cursor-key (:dao.stream/cursor r)) left)\n   989\t            state))\n   990\t\n   991\t        (not (pos? left)) state\n   992\t\n   993\t        :else\n   994\t        (let [r (stream/next reader cursor)\n   995\t              outcome (:dao.stream/outcome r)]\n   996\t          (cond\n   997\t            (= :dao.stream/ok outcome)\n   998\t            (recur (f (assoc state cursor-key (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   999\t                      (:dao.stream/value r))\n  1000\t                   (dec left))\n  1001\t\n  1002\t            (= :dao.stream/gap outcome)\n  1003\t            (recur (-> (assoc state cursor-key (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n  1004\t                       (fact {::fact ::gap, ::stream stream-name}))\n  1005\t                   (dec left))\n  1006\t\n  1007\t            :else state))))))\n  1008\t\n  1009\t\n  1010\t;; =============================================================================\n  1011\t;; Stage 4: advance pending work\n  1012\t;; =============================================================================\n  1013\t\n  1014\t(defn- expire-queries\n  1015\t  \"A query past query-ticks is a failed try: the peer's cookie is\n  1016\t   discarded (the query may have been dropped in silence), so the next try\n  1017\t   is a padded :ping; a peer out of tries is dead for that operation and\n  1018\t   leaves the table. A query sent before the first tick starts its clock\n  1019\t   at the first reading.\"\n  1020\t  [state]\n  1021\t  (let [now (:now state)]\n  1022\t    (reduce\n  1023\t      (fn [state [qkey {:keys [sent owner pkey]}]]\n  1024\t        (cond\n  1025\t          (nil? sent) (assoc-in state [:queries qkey :sent] now)\n  1026\t          (< (- now sent) (::query-ticks state)) state\n  1027\t          (nil? (op-record state owner)) (update state :queries dissoc qkey)\n  1028\t          :else\n  1029\t          (let [state (-> state\n  1030\t                          (update :queries dissoc qkey)\n  1031\t                          (update :cookies dissoc pkey)\n  1032\t                          (update-in (conj owner :failures pkey) (fnil inc 0)))]\n  1033\t            (if (>= (get-in state (conj owner :failures pkey)) (::tries state))\n  1034\t              (-> state\n  1035\t                  (update-in (conj owner :dead) conj pkey)\n  1036\t                  (update :table forget-address (first pkey) (second pkey)))\n  1037\t              state))))\n  1038\t      state\n  1039\t      (if now (:queries state) {}))))\n  1040\t\n  1041\t\n  1042\t(defn- advance\n  1043\t  [state]\n  1044\t  (let [state (expire-queries state)\n  1045\t        state (reduce (fn [state address]\n  1046\t                        (if (get-in state [:writes address])\n  1047\t                          (advance-write state address)\n  1048\t                          state))\n  1049\t                      state\n  1050\t                      (sort (keys (:writes state))))]\n  1051\t    (reduce (fn [state address]\n  1052\t              (if (get-in state [:gets address])\n  1053\t                (advance-get state address)\n  1054\t                state))\n  1055\t            state\n  1056\t            (sort (keys (:gets state))))))\n  1057\t\n  1058\t\n  1059\t;; =============================================================================\n  1060\t;; Stage 5 and the public surface\n  1061\t;; =============================================================================\n  1062\t\n  1063\t(defn- flush-out\n  1064\t  [state]\n  1065\t  (doseq [v (:out-answers state)] (stream/append! (:answers state) v))\n  1066\t  (doseq [v (:out-facts state)] (stream/append! (:facts state) v))\n  1067\t  (assoc state :out-answers [] :out-facts []))\n  1068\t\n  1069\t\n  1070\t(defn- defect\n  1071\t  \"A composition defect: the error, returned for the caller to throw.\"\n  1072\t  [message data]\n  1073\t  (ex-info (str \"dao.jing.dht: \" message) data))\n  1074\t\n  1075\t\n  1076\t(defn state\n  1077\t  \"Validate a composition (section 2) and return the DHT's state: a plain\n  1078\t   map of its handles, cursors, limits, routing table and pending tables.\n  1079\t   Throws on a composition defect; performs no stream operation.\"\n  1080\t  [composition]\n  1081\t  (let [c (merge defaults composition)\n  1082\t        {:keys [local requests answers facts ticks traffic datagrams]} c\n  1083\t        ack-peers (::ack-peers c)]\n  1084\t    (when-not (and (ifn? (:put-bytes-fn local)) (ifn? (:get-bytes-fn local)))\n  1085\t      (throw (defect \"composition needs a :local byte-store handle\"\n  1086\t                     {:local local})))\n  1087\t    (when-not (and requests (stream/reader? requests))\n  1088\t      (throw (defect \"composition needs a :requests reader\" {})))\n  1089\t    (when-not (and answers (stream/writer? answers))\n  1090\t      (throw (defect \"composition needs an :answers writer\" {})))\n  1091\t    (when-not (and facts (stream/writer? facts))\n  1092\t      (throw (defect \"composition needs a :facts writer\" {})))\n  1093\t    (when-not (and ticks (stream/reader? ticks))\n  1094\t      (throw (defect \"composition needs a :ticks reader\" {})))\n  1095\t    (when-not (= (some? traffic) (some? datagrams))\n  1096\t      (throw (defect \":traffic and :datagrams are composed together or not\"\n  1097\t                     {})))\n  1098\t    (when (and traffic\n  1099\t               (not (and (stream/reader? traffic) (stream/writer? datagrams))))\n  1100\t      (throw (defect \":traffic must be a reader and :datagrams a writer\" {})))\n  1101\t    (when-not (node-id? (::id c))\n  1102\t      (throw (defect \"the node id must be 64 lowercase hex characters\"\n  1103\t                     {:id (::id c)})))\n  1104\t    (when-not (and (integer? ack-peers) (<= 2 ack-peers kad/k))\n  1105\t      (throw (defect \"ack-peers must be an integer from 2 to k\"\n  1106\t                     {:ack-peers ack-peers, :k kad/k})))\n  1107\t    (merge c\n  1108\t           {:requests-cursor (get c :requests-cursor :dao.stream/oldest)\n  1109\t            :ticks-cursor (get c :ticks-cursor :dao.stream/oldest)\n  1110\t            :traffic-cursor (get c :traffic-cursor :dao.stream/oldest)\n  1111\t            :now nil\n  1112\t            :table {}\n  1113\t            :cookies {}\n  1114\t            :seen {}\n  1115\t            :queries {}\n  1116\t            :writes {}\n  1117\t            :gets {}\n  1118\t            :out-answers []\n  1119\t            :out-facts []})))\n  1120\t\n  1121\t\n  1122\t(defn step\n  1123\t  \"The only thing that advances the DHT, in section 2's order, each stage\n  1124\t   bounded by budget: drain ticks; read traffic; read requests; advance\n  1125\t   pending work; append answers and facts. Returns the successor state.\n  1126\t   This is an interpreter step -- it performs stream operations -- under\n  1127\t   a single-owner precondition: one caller, one state thread.\"\n  1128\t  [state budget]\n  1129\t  (-> state\n  1130\t      (drain :ticks :ticks-cursor :ticks budget on-tick)\n  1131\t      (cond-> (:traffic state)\n  1132\t        (drain :traffic :traffic-cursor :traffic budget on-traffic))\n  1133\t      (drain :requests :requests-cursor :requests budget on-request-value)\n  1134\t      (cond-> (not (solo? state)) advance)\n  1135\t      flush-out))\n  1136\t\n  1137\t\n  1138\t;; =============================================================================\n  1139\t;; Section 5.1: the byte-store handle\n  1140\t;; =============================================================================\n  1141\t\n  1142\t(defn store-handle\n  1143\t  \"The plain-data dao.jing byte-store handle over a DHT composition's\n  1144\t   :local and :requests: put-bytes-fn validates, refuses an oversize store\n  1145\t   message, inserts into :local, appends {:dao.jing.dht/replicate address}\n  1146\t   and returns the local verdict at once -- never the acknowledgement,\n  1147\t   which is the :dao.jing.dht/sent fact. get-bytes-fn reads :local only\n  1148\t   and never touches the network; close-fn closes :local.\"\n  1149\t  [{:keys [local requests max-message-bytes]}]\n  1150\t  (when-not (and (ifn? (:put-bytes-fn local)) (ifn? (:get-bytes-fn local)))\n  1151\t    (throw (defect \"store-handle needs a :local byte-store handle\"\n  1152\t                   {:local local})))\n  1153\t  (when-not (and requests (stream/writer? requests))\n  1154\t    (throw (defect \"store-handle needs a :requests writer\" {})))\n  1155\t  (let [limit (or max-message-bytes (::max-message-bytes defaults))]\n  1156\t    {:local local\n  1157\t     :requests requests\n  1158\t     :put-bytes-fn\n  1159\t     (fn [address bs]\n  1160\t       (when-not (jing/segment-bytes-match? address bs)\n  1161\t         (throw (defect \"content address does not match the bytes\"\n  1162\t                        {:address address})))\n  1163\t       (when (oversize? limit address bs)\n  1164\t         (throw (defect \"the store message exceeds max-message-bytes\"\n  1165\t                        {:address address, :reason ::oversize,\n  1166\t                         :max-message-bytes limit})))\n  1167\t       (let [verdict ((:put-bytes-fn local) address bs)]\n  1168\t         (stream/append! requests {::replicate address})\n  1169\t         verdict))\n  1170\t     :get-bytes-fn (fn [address not-found]\n  1171\t                     ((:get-bytes-fn local) address not-found))\n  1172\t     :close-fn (fn [] (jing/close! local))}))\n  1173\t\n  1174\t\n  1175\t;; =============================================================================\n  1176\t;; LEGACY (pending an Architect ruling; see the S2 report): the waiting\n  1177\t;; transport surface the contract deletes in S2. dao.jing.dht.node, which\n  1178\t;; the contract deletes in S3, still implements IDhtNet and calls lookup and\n  1179\t;; create-content-dht, so deleting them here breaks the JVM build until S3.\n  1180\t;; =============================================================================\n  1181\t\n  1182\t;; =============================================================================\n  1183\t;; Routing identity\n  1184\t;; =============================================================================\n  1185\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790762091000-orchestrator-dao-jing-dht-epic-owner-decisions.md; cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790764302000-storage-engineer-dht-s2-core.claude-opus-5-5.report.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-Local: 2026-09-30 16:54:51 +07\nCoding-Agent: interactive\nSession-ID: not-applicable (interactive seat)\n# dao.jing.dht epic — OWNER DECISIONS (verbatim), after mob synthesis + ratification\n\nDesign: collab/1790750376000-architect-dao-jing-dht-epic-mob-synthesis.gpt-6-sol.findings.md; ratified by gemini-3.1-pro-high\n(RATIFY) and glm-5.3 (RATIFY-WITH-CONDITIONS: S0 disambiguate raw descriptor local-bind keys vs UDP channel\nremote-destination keys; S3 acceptance criterion \"shared chunk utility used by both\" with a declared DHT-owned-reassembly\nfallback). Final fable sign-off dispatched (collab/1790761753000-architect-dao-jing-dht-epic-fable-signoff.prompt.md).\n\n1. Publication before ShiBi — selected: \"Explicit opt-in allowed (Recommended) — Default: never publish. A separate flag,\n   distinct from configuring peers, allows publishing that code index; the REPL states what will be shared.\"\n2. Acknowledgement — first answer: \"i want to take the kafka route. write is acknowledged immediately as long as it is sent\n   out on a network. this works because the data is written to a peer\". Clarified: ack level = \"sent to a peer but it\n   must send to multiple peers before it can be considered ack\"; local copy = \"Yes, local + network — Local durable insert\n   as today, then the network write per the ack level above.\"\n   => SUPERSEDES mob D3 (local ack + volatile best-effort replication). Open for the Architect: the number of peers\n   (\"multiple\"), behaviour with fewer reachable peers (incl. solo mode), and reconciling with D8 (no synchronous lookup\n   stalling REPL rounds).\n3. Root discovery — selected: \"Ratify (Recommended) — Keep this epic's scope; queue root discovery separately.\"\n4. Compatibility — selected: \"Ratify (Recommended) — Changes today's synchronous DHT miss behavior; the JVM facade bridges\n   callers that need blocking.\"\n\n5. (2026-09-30 17:21:35 +07) ack-peers — owner, verbatim: \"i change my mind. a min of 2 peers not 3\". Matches fable's S0 (default 2, floor 2,\n   ceiling k=20); no contract change needed.\n6. (2026-09-30 17:23:41 +07) No-publish behaviour — selected: \"Fetch-only (Recommended) — Fable's S0: refuses inbound stores and serves nothing;\n   still routes and caches what it asks for. A pure consumer until you opt in.\"\n7. (2026-09-30 17:23:41 +07) S0 behaviours — selected: \"Confirm all (Recommended)\": (a) acked = sent to nearest already-known peers, k-nearest\n   replication best-effort after; (b) solo never acknowledges; (c) oversize refused before the local insert (64 KiB\n   default, measured in S3).\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-09-30 11:08:10 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-09-30 18:08:10 +07\nCoding-Agent: claude\nSession-ID: eb3d451a-74ba-462d-8788-df45ee5c25f8\n# Report: DHT epic S2 — caller-stepped DHT core on in-memory sockets\n\nWorktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-dht-s2 (branch dht-s2 from dac64b41). Nothing staged or committed.\n\n## STOP ITEM FOR THE ARCHITECT (contract inconsistency, section 10)\n\nThe contract says `dao.jing.dht/IDhtNet`, `lookup` and `create-content-dht` are **deleted in S2**, and\n`dao.jing.dht.node` is **deleted in S3**. But `src/cljc/dao/jing/dht/node.cljc` (S3's to delete) implements\n`dht/IDhtNet` (line 254) and calls `dht/lookup` (331), `dht/create-content-dht` (344) and `dht/node-id` (312), and\n`test/dao/jing/dht/node_test.cljc` calls `dht/self-peer`, `dht/fetch-content`, `dht/find-closer`,\n`dht/store-content!`, `dht/close-net!`. Deleting the three in S2 breaks the JVM lane (`clj -M:test` loads node_test →\nnode) until S3 lands. I did **not** reinterpret this: the waiting surface is left in place, at the bottom of\n`dao.jing.dht`, under a `LEGACY (pending an Architect ruling)` banner; everything else in S2 is done and does not\ndepend on it. Resolutions the Architect can pick from:\n(a) move `dao.jing.dht.node` + `node_test` deletion into S2 (no UDP DHT between S2 and S3; dev repo, no fleet);\n(b) keep the legacy surface until S3 deletes node, and amend the section-10 table;\n(c) move the protocol and its helpers into `dao.jing.dht.node` in S2 (a small move, node self-contained until S3).\nOnce ruled, (a) or (b)/(c) is a ~10-minute follow-up. `dao.jing.md` states this pending status.\n\n## What was built\n\n- `src/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc` (portable CLJC): `state` (composition validation: ack-peers 2..k, handles, id,\n  traffic/datagrams both or neither; performs no stream op), `step` (section 2 order: ticks → traffic → requests →\n  advance → append answers/facts; each read stage bounded by budget; gap adopts recovery cursor and appends\n  `/gap`). Pending writes (warm ack in the reading step after exactly ack-peers sends; cold lookup + pings;\n  `/sent`, `/unacknowledged` with all six reasons, post-ack best-effort replication to k and `/replicated` with\n  `/confirmed`), pending gets (local hit same step; lookup + fetch ≤ alpha; strict verify via\n  `dao.jing/accept-bytes!`; cache in :local; `/miss` exhausted/deadline/solo/busy). Lookup as explicit state\n  (candidates = table nearest + bootstrap + `:find` hints; answered/dead sets; per-peer tries; dead peers leave the\n  table). Section 7 wire through `dao.stream.cbor`, single-datagram only; replies matched by `[observed host, port,\n  :q]`; entries only from matched full replies or valid-cookie requests, observed address only. The whole section-8\n  cookie protocol: issue on every reply, echo, stateless verify (current or previous epoch), the gate (no work, no\n  entry, no storage), the size rule (need-cookie only if ≤ the causing datagram, else silence), first-contact padding\n  to ≥256, need-cookie recovery (re-send once, no try consumed), timeout → discard cookie → padded ping, freshness.\n  `cookie-for` is the S2 stand-in, public so tests predict it. `publish?` false: writes `/unpublished`, inbound\n  store `:ok false`, fetch not found, still answers ping/find and fetches/caches. `store-handle`: validate, oversize\n  throw (ex-data `:reason :dao.jing.dht/oversize`) before insert, local insert, one replicate append, local verdict;\n  get :local only; close closes :local. Base64 only via `dao.jing/bytes->base64` / `base64->bytes`.\n- `src/cljc/dao/jing/content/step.cljc`: `unacknowledged-code`; the exact answer `{:jing/request r\n  :jing/unacknowledged reason}` completes as `{:id id :error {:code :dao.jing.content/unacknowledged :reason\n  reason}}` (plain put and materialization put; extra keys stay malformed).\n- `src/clj/dao/jing/dht/facade.clj` (JVM only): `start!` owns one daemon driver thread = the state's one step owner\n  and tick cadence (monotonic ms since start); get miss → `dao.jing.content.driver` waits to its request deadline;\n  put is the store handle's (local verdict, no wait); close stops/joins the thread, closes the pair and :local.\n- `test/dao/jing/dht/mesh.cljc` (test support): ring-buffer traffic per node + a `MeshSocket` writer carrying raw\n  datagram values (section 2 shapes), logging, loss via `:drop?`. No socket, no S1.\n- Rewrites: `test/dao/jing/dht_test.cljc` (21 tests / 133 assertions), `test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc` fake\n  `GridNet` → `dht-runtime` (node 1's request/answer pair *is* the linker's content pair; peers seeded with forged\n  or honest bytes), and **also `test/yin/vm/linker_step_test.cljc`**, whose DHT test used `lt/grid-handle` /\n  `lt/any-address` (not named in the brief, but it consumed the deleted fake net, so it had to move with it).\n- `docs/design/dao.jing.md`: backend list entry and status for `dao.jing.dht` (S2), and the Base64 sentence (DHT\n  wire uses CBOR byte strings; Base64 only in stream-visible values).\n- Not touched: dao.stream.datagram / dao.stream.udp / yin/repl/*, `dao.jing.dht.kad`, `dao.jing.dht.node`.\n\n## Acceptance bullets → tests (dht_test unless noted)\n\n- Acked write used each counted peer's fresh-reply cookie; missing/wrong cookie store causes no work:\n  `warm-table-write-is-acknowledged-in-the-step-that-reads-it`, `the-gate-answers-need-cookie-or-silence`.\n- Need-cookie ≤ first-contact-bytes; short cookie-less datagram → silence: `need-cookie-reply-never-exceeds-first-\n  contact-bytes`, `the-gate-…`, `first-contact-is-a-padded-ping`.\n- Exact `:jing/*` shapes, unmodified clients drive a DHT: `the-unmodified-content-client-materializes-through-a-dht`\n  (`:inserted`, then `:present` via the verify read), `a-remote-read-is-verified-and-cached`, cold-bootstrap test\n  (unacknowledged completion), linker tests; `content.step-test/an-unacknowledged-put-completes-with-its-reason`.\n- Warm table: acked in the reading step after exactly ack-peers sends, `/sent`: warm test.\n- put-bytes-fn no lookup/no wait; publish/readback against :local: `the-store-handle-returns-the-local-verdict-at-once`.\n- Every `/unacknowledged` reason incl. cold bootstrap too-few-peers at the tick deadline then success:\n  `every-at-once-unacknowledged-reason` (solo, unpublished, oversize ×2 modes, absent, busy),\n  `cold-bootstrap-reaches-too-few-peers-then-succeeds`, `a-query-that-times-out-is-retried-then-its-peer-is-dead`.\n- Solo composes no socket streams, holds no pending work: `every-at-once-…` (solo block).\n- File-backed local verdict survives restart: `a-file-backed-local-verdict-survives-restart` (all three hosts).\n- Time only by appended ticks; no test sleeps: `time-advances-only-by-appended-ticks`; no sleep anywhere in tests.\n- JVM facade one step owner, respects deadlines: `dao.jing.dht.facade-test` (with-redefs counts stepping threads:\n  exactly 2 facades → 2 threads, never the caller; 150 ms driver timeout returns well under get-ticks).\n- dao.jing.md backend list and status updated.\n\n## Red phase (unmodified tree, tests first)\n\n- `clojure -M:test -n dao.jing.dht-test` → `Syntax error … No such var: dht/decode-message` (mesh.cljc).\n- `-n dao.jing.content.step-test` → `FAIL in (an-unacknowledged-put-completes-with-its-reason) (step_test.cljc:720)`,\n  18 tests, 1 failure.\n- `-n dao.jing.dht.facade-test` → `Could not locate dao/jing/dht/facade…`.\n\n## Mutation proofs (each applied, suite run, reverted; `grep` confirms 0 residue; `git diff --stat src` unchanged)\n\n| Mutation | Caught by |\n|---|---|\n| M1 gate accepts any cookie | the-gate (6+ assertions) |\n| M2 ack threshold dec (equivalent in warm case) | timeout/dead-peer test; sharper M2b below |\n| M2b send only 1 store before ack | warm test (6), stale, timeout |\n| M3 need-cookie ignores the size rule | the-gate (2) |\n| M4 every peer fresh | stale-peer (2), timeout |\n| M5 fetched bytes unverified | forged-payload test (error) |\n| M6 no unacknowledged completion in content.step | step_test:720 |\n| M7b store echoes a cookie no reply carried | warm test cookie assertions (4), stale |\n(M7 as first written was overwritten by the real cookie, so a no-op; replaced by M7b.)\n\n## Checks (all foreground, in the worktree)\n\n- `clj -M:kondo --lint` on all 9 changed/new files: errors 0, warnings 0.\n- `cljstyle check …`: **blocked** by the session permission gate (command required approval; not run).\n- Focused JVM: dht-test 21/133, content.step-test, facade-test, linker-test, linker-step-test: 0 failures.\n- Full `clojure -M:test`: Ran 2409 tests, 184884 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- `bb test:cljs`: Ran 2311 tests, 51247 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors (dht-test, content.step-test, linker tests\n  listed as \"Testing …\").\n- `bb test:cljd`: `+2273: All tests passed!`; all 21 `dao.jing.dht-test` vars and the new content.step test ran.\n\n## Interpretive choices the Architect should confirm (none changes the wire or the contract's rules)\n\n1. A need-cookie reply stores the cookie but does not prove or freshen the peer; only a full matched reply records\n   the entry and sets freshness. First contact is therefore ping → need-cookie → ping(cookie) → ok.\n2. An operation (or query) created before any tick starts its clock at the first observed reading (\"a step that has\n   observed no tick expires nothing\").\n3. `cookie-for` hashes the UTF-8 string `\"<epoch>|<host>|<port>\"` (the contract's `|` read literally).\n4. Freshness is `now - seen < cookie-epoch-ticks`.\n5. After the ack the same step stops; replication (stores to the remaining k nearest, the finishing lookup) begins on\n   the next step, so the reading step sends exactly ack-peers stores. The replication deadline reuses ack-ticks from\n   the write's start.\n6. A `:jing/put` joining a write already acknowledged is answered at once with its own local verdict.\n7. `/local` is nil for replicate requests and for oversize (no insert); `/gap`'s `/stream` is `:requests`,\n   `:traffic` or `:ticks`.\n8. Tries are counted per (operation, peer); a peer out of tries is dead for that op and removed from the table. One\n   outstanding query per (op, peer); pings for stale store targets capped at alpha.\n9. Composition cursor keys are `:requests-cursor`, `:ticks-cursor`, `:traffic-cursor`, default `:dao.stream/oldest`.\n10. The store handle ignores the replicate append's outcome (a ring only refuses when closed).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
